---
import core from '../../../lib/relational-collection/core.json';
const later=[{order_id:105,placed_at:'2026-10-21T12:00:00Z'},{order_id:106,placed_at:'2026-10-21T12:00:00Z'}];
const rows=[...core.orders,...later];
---
<figure class="frame-figure" data-frame aria-labelledby="r06-frame-title">
 <figcaption id="r06-frame-title"><span>Figure 2</span> Which rows does this count include?</figcaption>
 <div class="options"><label>Frame <select data-frame-mode><option value="range">Default RANGE</option><option value="rows">ROWS, with tie-breaker</option><option value="all">Whole partition</option></select></label><label>Current order <select data-current><option value="105">105</option><option value="106">106</option></select></label></div>
 <p class="expression" data-expression>count(*) OVER (ORDER BY placed_at)</p>
 <table><caption>The five-order illustration, shown in time and ID order</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Order</th><th scope="col">Placed (UTC)</th><th scope="col">Frame</th></tr></thead><tbody>{rows.map(o=><tr data-order={o.order_id} data-included="true" data-current-row={o.order_id===105?'true':'false'}><th scope="row">{o.order_id}<span data-cursor>{o.order_id===105?' ← current':''}</span></th><td>{o.placed_at.replace('2026-','').replace('T',' ').replace(':00Z','')}</td><td data-status>included</td></tr>)}</tbody></table>
 <p class="count">Count at this row: <strong data-count>5</strong></p>
 <p data-explanation aria-live="polite">Orders 105 and 106 have the same placed_at. The default ordered frame reaches through both peers, so the count at 105 already includes 106.</p>
 <details><summary>Frame membership as text</summary><p>For current order 105, default RANGE includes 101, 102, 103, 105 and 106, a count of five. ROWS ordered by placed_at and order_id includes only 101, 102, 103 and 105, a count of four. At 106 both frames count five. The whole-partition count is five at either row. No amounts or order lines are assumed for the later two orders.</p></details>
</figure>
<script>
 document.querySelectorAll('[data-frame]').forEach(root=>{
 const mode=root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-frame-mode]')!,current=root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-current]')!;
 const draw=()=>{const id=Number(current.value),m=mode.value;let count=0;
 root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-order]').forEach(r=>{const rid=Number(r.dataset.order),inside=m!=='rows'||rid<=id;r.dataset.included=String(inside);r.dataset.currentRow=String(rid===id);r.querySelector('[data-cursor]')!.textContent=rid===id?' ← current':'';r.querySelector('[data-status]')!.textContent=inside?'included':'outside';if(inside)count++;});
 root.querySelector('[data-count]')!.textContent=String(count);
 root.querySelector('[data-expression]')!.textContent=m==='range'?'count(*) OVER (ORDER BY placed_at)':m==='rows'?'count(*) OVER (ORDER BY placed_at, order_id ROWS BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW)':'count(*) OVER ()';
 root.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=m==='range'?`Orders 105 and 106 have the same placed_at. The default ordered frame reaches through both peers, so the count at ${id} includes both.`:m==='rows'?`The tie-breaker puts 105 before 106. ROWS stops at the current row, ${id}, so ${count} rows contribute.`:'Without an order in OVER, the default frame is the whole partition. All five rows contribute at every current row.';
 };mode.addEventListener('change',draw);current.addEventListener('change',draw);draw();
 });
</script>
<style>
.frame-figure{margin:2.5rem 0;padding:1rem;background:var(--color-surface-alt);border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);font:.9rem/1.6 var(--font-sans)}figcaption{font-size:1.08rem;margin-bottom:1rem}figcaption span{font-size:.75rem;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--color-text-secondary);margin-right:.6rem}.options{display:flex;gap:1rem;flex-wrap:wrap}.options label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.3rem}select{font:inherit;padding:.5rem;max-width:100%;color:var(--color-text);background:var(--color-surface);border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);border-radius:.25rem}select:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--color-accent);outline-offset:3px}.expression{font:.8rem/1.6 var(--font-mono);min-height:5em;overflow-wrap:anywhere}table{display:table;width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.82rem}td,th{padding:.55rem .35rem;text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong)}caption{font-size:.8rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary);text-align:left;margin-bottom:.6rem}tr[data-current-row="true"]{outline:2px solid var(--color-accent);outline-offset:-2px}tr[data-included="true"] td:last-child{color:var(--color-accent);font-weight:650}.count{font-size:1.05rem}.count strong{font-size:1.5rem;color:var(--color-accent)}[data-explanation]{min-height:6em;border-left:3px solid var(--color-accent);padding-left:.7rem}details{font-size:.85rem}@media(max-width:430px){.frame-figure{padding:.7rem}td,th{padding:.6rem .25rem;font-size:.75rem}[data-cursor]{display:block}}
</style>
